# Leave this EMPTY (or delete the file) for both local development and the
# normal Vercel deployment.
#
# Why: the client and the API are served from the same origin, so the app calls
# the relative path /api. Locally, Vite proxies /api to http://localhost:5000
# (see vite.config.js). On Vercel, /api is the serverless function in api/.
# Either way there is no URL to keep in sync and no CORS to configure.
#
# Only set this if you host the API somewhere else — then give the full URL
# ending in /api, e.g.
#   VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.vercel.app/api
#
# A localhost value is deliberately ignored once the page is not on localhost,
# so a stale build can never send a live visitor's login to your laptop.
#
# Vite only reads this file at startup — restart `npm run dev` after changing it.
VITE_API_URL=
